STEP 1 OWNERSHIP PROBE — GO. Measured 2026-09-09 by worker-a11dcf70 against docker Server 29.6.2, image node:24.16.0-alpine (digest sha256:21f403ab171f2dc89bad4dd69d7721bfd15f084ccb46cdd225f31f2bc59b5c9a).

MEASUREMENTS
- `docker run --rm node:24.16.0-alpine id -u node` => 1000; `id -g node` => 1000. The plan's "uid/gid 1000 is a LEAD not a measurement" is now a measurement.
- `/run` EXISTS in the image (`drwxr-xr-x 3 root root /run`). `/run/moe` DOES NOT (`ls: /run/moe: No such file or directory`).
- THE DECIDING RESULT: `docker cp - <container>:/` HONOURS the USTAR header's uid/gid WITHOUT `-a`/`--archive`. A file entry with uid=1000 gid=1000 mode=0600 landed as `-rw------- 1 1000 1000 /run/moe/env` and `docker exec`-equivalent read-back AS THE node USER printed the payload.
- COUNTERFACTUAL (the control that makes the above non-vacuous): the SAME archive with uid=0 gid=0 in the headers landed as `-rw------- 1 0 0` and the node user got `cat: can't open '/run/moe/env': Permission denied`, rc=1. So the header fields DRIVE ownership; they are not decoration and docker is not chowning to the container's --user.
- Both dir-entry shapes work: `run/moe/` + `run/moe/env` (explicit), and `run/moe/env` alone (docker auto-creates the intermediate dir). CHOSEN: the EXPLICIT `run/moe/` entry at 0755 uid/gid 1000, because it is the shape actually measured end-to-end and does not depend on an undocumented auto-create.
- `docker cp - <absent-container>:/` REFUSES: stderr `destination "moe-probe-does-not-exist:/" must be a directory`, EXIT 1. That is the refusal shape step 3's double models.
- bsdtar read-back of the same bytes: `tar -tvf -` EXIT 0 listing `drwxr-xr-x 1000/1000 run/moe/` and `-rw------- 1000/1000 31 run/moe/env`; `tar -xOf - run/moe/env` EXIT 0 returning the exact payload.

PINNED FOR LATER STEPS: destination `/`, no `-a` flag, uid=1000, gid=1000, file mode 0600, dir mode 0755, dest path /run/moe/env (already `CANDIDATE_ENVIRONMENT_PATH`).

TEARDOWN (epic rail 4): all four probe containers removed; `docker ps -a --filter name=moe-probe` returns EMPTY.

PROBE SOURCE, inline so a grader can recreate it (out-of-tree scratch, %TEMP%/moe-task-60f851fa3e-probe/tarprobe.mjs, nothing written into the repo):
```js
const BLOCK = 512;
function octal(value, width) { return value.toString(8).padStart(width - 1, "0") + "\0"; }
function header({ name, mode, uid, gid, size, mtime, typeflag }) {
  const b = Buffer.alloc(BLOCK, 0);
  b.write(name, 0, 100, "utf8");
  b.write(octal(mode, 8), 100, 8, "ascii");
  b.write(octal(uid, 8), 108, 8, "ascii");
  b.write(octal(gid, 8), 116, 8, "ascii");
  b.write(octal(size, 12), 124, 12, "ascii");
  b.write(octal(mtime, 12), 136, 12, "ascii");
  b.write("        ", 148, 8, "ascii");
  b.write(typeflag, 156, 1, "ascii");
  b.write("ustar\0", 257, 6, "ascii");
  b.write("00", 263, 2, "ascii");
  let sum = 0; for (const byte of b) sum += byte;
  b.write(octal(sum, 7) + " ", 148, 8, "ascii");
  return b;
}
const payload = Buffer.from("SECRET_TOKEN='probe-value-abc'\n", "utf8");
const parts = [
  header({ name: "run/moe/", mode: 0o755, uid: 1000, gid: 1000, size: 0, mtime: 0, typeflag: "5" }),
  header({ name: "run/moe/env", mode: 0o600, uid: 1000, gid: 1000, size: payload.length, mtime: 0, typeflag: "0" }),
  payload,
  Buffer.alloc((BLOCK - (payload.length % BLOCK)) % BLOCK, 0),
  Buffer.alloc(BLOCK * 2, 0),
];
process.stdout.write(Buffer.concat(parts));
```
Reproduce: `node tarprobe.mjs > probe.tar`; `docker create --user node --name c node:24.16.0-alpine sh -c 'ls -ln /run/moe/env; cat /run/moe/env'`; `docker cp - c:/ < probe.tar`; `docker start -a c`; `docker rm -f c`.
